  "bodyHtml": "\n\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-168842638426899e3410/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>Michael Rudden</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2024-03-26T15:11:14-04:00\" title=\"Tuesday, March 26, 2024, 3:11 pm\">March 26, 2024</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t<p>On a recent sunny Saturday members of the Guild of Harwich Artists gathered in Doane Park in Harwich Port to celebrate <img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-6749\" src=\"/media/archive/6d458e30b9d9b042227afff3c61498071e4f59167a22cb87f4454ebf06af67f1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"142\" loading=\"lazy\" /> (age 100), a co-founding member of the Guild.  The impetus for the gathering was the recent installation of a park bench that commemorates the founding of the Guild by local artists who started selling their art in Doane Park in the mid-1970’s.  The Guild’s Monday ‘Art-in-the-Park’ during the summer season continues to this day. Proceeds to purchase the oak bench were raised in a silent auction of Vivien’s art in the park last September.</p>\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<footer class=\"entry-footer\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-terms category\">Posted in <a href=\"/archive/source-a2dd2a8b0cc8efdccc38/\" rel=\"tag\">MEET THE ARTIST</a></span>\t\t\t<br /><span class=\"entry-terms post_tag\">Tagged <a href=\"/archive/source-b192a62ef6f202943428/\" rel=\"tag\">Vivien Oswell's Bench</a></span>\t\t</footer>\n\n\t\n",
